// PLEXIL baseline -- Mission A, model-covered case (execution_plan §11.1, §21.5).
//
// "PDU-2 reported a fault: restore it, verify, return the rover to the dock with the arm stowed." In the covered
// case the reported unit is the faulted one and its reset button is free, so the pre-engineered procedure is:
// drive to the unit, dock at its panel, press the reset button, stow, return to the dock.
//
// Rewritten onto the shared whole-operation `press` capability (2026-09-22; research repo F92-F100 fixed the arm
// that made this worth doing, F104 fixed the adapter bug that would have raced it to "done" before the robot
// moved). The previous version bypassed `press` with eight stage-level Cartesian primitives of its own
// (close jaws, plan/servo pre-press, approach, press, retract, re-ready, ...) -- `press`'s own contract already
// does exactly that sequence internally ("the jaws close, the tool goes in past the button's tip ... then
// withdraws and the jaws open") and explicitly does not need `arm_ready` first ("this plans its own way from
// wherever the arm is, so arm_ready beforehand is neither required nor useful",
// openral_ext/capability_server/contracts.yaml). Ours' own covered-instance call (research repo
// artifacts/runs/mission_a_success_20260922/ours/events.jsonl) called `arm_ready` anyway and it failed --
// harmlessly, exactly because press does not need it -- not repeated here. Composed from the same reusable
// library Mission B uses (`DriveAndDock`, `StowAndReturn` -- baselines/plexil/plans/lib/), not duplicated.

LibraryAction DriveAndDock(In String feature, In Real standoff_m, In Real approach_m, InOut Boolean ok);
LibraryAction StowAndReturn(In Real dock_x, In Real dock_y, In Real dock_yaw, InOut Boolean ok);
Boolean Command press(String, String);
String Lookup LastCapabilityResult();
Command pprint(...);

MissionA_Covered: Sequence
{
  String Button = "pdu_2_panel/press";
  String ButtonTarget = "the round red push button set into the yellow sub-panel";
  Boolean ok = true;

  ToUnit: { PreCondition ok; LibraryCall DriveAndDock(feature = Button, standoff_m = 1.5, approach_m = 1.5, ok = ok); }
  Press:  { PreCondition ok; EndCondition isKnown(ok); PostCondition ok; ok = press(ButtonTarget, Button); }
  Return: { PreCondition ok; LibraryCall StowAndReturn(dock_x = 0.0, dock_y = 0.0, dock_yaw = 0.0, ok = ok); }
  Done: { pprint("MissionA_Covered ok:", ok, "last:", Lookup(LastCapabilityResult())); }
}
